2026-11-06T03:00:26.4525580Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4533445Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4534077Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4534802Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4535060Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4535348Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4535622Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4535960Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4536444Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4536725Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4536844Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4537344Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4537632Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4537860Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4538406Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:00:26.4538638Z 
